# Normalise line endings in the repository, not on each checkout.
#
# The blobs have always been LF; editors and scripts on Windows kept rewriting
# them to CRLF, which turns a one-line change into a 260-line diff and makes
# review useless. Everything is stored LF and checked out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell files are stored LF too. Windows PowerShell reads a BOM-less UTF-8
# script using the system code page, so scripts that contain non-ASCII text carry
# a BOM - that rule is about encoding, not line endings, and the two are separate.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=lf

# Binary formats: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.msix binary
*.pfx binary
*.cer binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.sys binary
*.vmdk binary
*.iso binary